    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That sounds better, but I'm looking at the specific wording you suggested. If we tell them \"the carrier logs showed no damage,\" isn't that essentially calling them a liar? I'm worried that if we're too honest about the sensor data, they'll just get angry and fight harder for the chargeback. \n\nInstead of mentioning the carrier logs at all, can we just tell them that we've decided to approve the refund as a one-time courtesy to keep things simple? It seems like a cleaner way to shut down the dispute without making it an argument about who is right. What do you think?",
